{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"39235b5ef736285fe1ad8be152f74d149e6dede4cb5416a5916582f5fdd94a44","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / guide criterion parity","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/plan_review/guide_parity.py","src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py","validate_guide_criterion_pins()","regenerate_guide_criterion_pins()","cited_criteria()","CANONICAL_LLM","AUTHOR_GUIDES","CONTRIBUTING.md","tests/unit/test_guides.py"],"problem_keywords":["criterion drift","guide parity","prose accuracy","citation validation","registry synchronization"],"propositions":["A prose guide cites criterion ids from the registry but the cited criterion text can change silently, leaving paraphrased claims in the guide stranded and incorrect.","No systematic coupling exists between the 20 cited criteria in packaged prose guides and the registry; only G6 has hand-written parity tests that caught bug 828a after a month in production.","The gate must pin criterion digests at guide-cite time, fail on text drift with a visible reminder to re-verify the guide's claim, and run in CI without a new workflow step.","Citation extraction must be vocabulary-only (word-boundary matching against CANONICAL_LLM) and structure-agnostic so that ordinary prose edits and guide restructures do not break the gate."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787888836313400001,"uuid":"8c0cc925-7517-4a46-9726-411493f9233f"}